{
  "slug": "cod-white-bean-dinner-skillet",
  "name": "Cod and bean skillet",
  "description": "Cod fillet braised on a bed of canned kidney beans with tomato, onion and garlic, spinach folded in at the end. Any mild canned bean works in place of the kidney beans.",
  "iconKey": "pot",
  "instructions": [
    "Warm the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion until soft, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add the garlic and the diced tomato and cook until the tomato breaks down, about 5 minutes.",
    "Drain and rinse the kidney beans, stir them in with the black pepper and let them warm through.",
    "Lay the cod fillet on top, cover the pan and cook until the fish is opaque and flakes easily, about 8 minutes.",
    "Fold the spinach through the beans until it wilts, then serve each plate with a piece of the cod."
